{"type": "survey_submit", "survey_type": "post", "puzzle_idx": null, "answers": {"puzzle_1_rate_again": 4, "puzzle_1_guesses": "many", "puzzle_2_rate_again": 4, "puzzle_2_guesses": "few", "puzzle_3_rate_again": 3, "puzzle_3_guesses": "few", "strategy": "Starting with the row/column with the largest sum or the largest # of #s (determining which squares MUST be black / MUST be white) and then making a few educated guesses until I encountered a contradiction", "comments": "The puzzles felt easier when I was given hints, since it let me determine whether the previous guesses I made were correct or incorrect (more often incorrect ...) or maybe I made too many guesses", "puzzle_3_rating_reason": "I thought this puzzle was easier than the first 2 (took me less time) and the 2 columns with 1 and 8 easily ruled out 2 columns. The columns beside each other also made it easy to make an educated guess about what squares I thought should be black/white. ", "puzzle_1_rating_reason": "Hard. I found myself waiting to use the Hint button because I was struggling to determine whether or not a box was white/black without making any guesses. I tried to refrain from making guesses until the Hint button was available", "puzzle_2_rating_reason": "I found the difficulty just as hard as the first one, with a lot of guessing and checking (with the Hint button)"}, "t": "2026-06-04T20:40:14.887526+00:00"}
